Rep-Hakeem-Jeffries-Official-Portrait-1638x2048_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rep-Hakeem-Jeffries-Official-Portrait-1638x2048_(cropped).jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Rep-Hakeem-Jeffries-Official-Portrait-1638x2048_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Rep-Hakeem-Jeffries-Official-Portrait-1638x2048_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Rep-Hakeem-Jeffries-Official-Portrait-1638x2048_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Rep-Hakeem-Jeffries-Official-Portrait-1638x2048_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1968\" data-file-height=\"2576\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"200\" width=\"153\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Leader</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Johnson\" title=\"Mike Johnson\">Mike Johnson</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hakeem_Jeffries\" title=\"Hakeem Jeffries\">Hakeem Jeffries</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(US)\" title=\"Republican Party (US)\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Republican</a></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(US)\" title=\"Democratic Party (US)\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Democratic</a></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Leader<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>since</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">October 25, 2023</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">January 3, 2023</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Leader's<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>seat</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><span data-sort-value=\"Louisiana04 !\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana's_4th_congressional_district\" title=\"Louisiana's 4th congressional district\">Louisiana<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>4th</a></span></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><span data-sort-value=\"New York08 !\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York's_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"New York's 8th congressional district\">New York<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>8th</a></span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Last<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>election</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">220 seats, 49.8%</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">215 seats, 47.2%</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Current<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>seats</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">218<sup about=\"#mwt12\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Independents1_2-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Independents1\",\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"html\":\"\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Independents1-2\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwEA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwEQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwEg\">[</span>b<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwEw\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">214</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Seats<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>needed</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\"}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\"}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 4</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\"><hr/></td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #DDDDBB;\"></td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;width:0;;\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_(US)\" title=\"Independent (US)\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Independent</a></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Last<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>election</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">0 seats</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Current<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>seats</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">1<sup about=\"#mwt14\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Independents1_2-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Independents1\",\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Independents1-2\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Independents1-2\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwFA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwFQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFg\">[</span>b<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwFw\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Seats<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>needed</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\"}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\"></td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_retirements_or_losses_of_renomination_map.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_retirements_or_losses_of_renomination_map.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_retirements_or_losses_of_renomination_map.svg/500px-2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_retirements_or_losses_of_renomination_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_retirements_or_losses_of_renomination_map.svg/960px-2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_retirements_or_losses_of_renomination_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"512\" data-file-height=\"318\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"217\" width=\"350\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></a></span><div><span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#92C5DE; color:#92C5DE;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Democratic incumbent</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#0671B0; color:#0671B0;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Democratic incumbent retiring or lost renomination</span><br/><span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#F48882; color:#F48882;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Republican incumbent</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#CA0120; color:#CA0120;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Republican incumbent retiring, lost renomination, or withdrew</span><br/><span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#999999; color:#999999;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Independent incumbent</span><br/><span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6D6D6D; color:#6D6D6D;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>No incumbent</span><sup about=\"#mwt16\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-3\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-3\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwGA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwGQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwGg\">[</span>c<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwGw\">]</span></span></a></sup> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#808080; color:#808080;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Vacant</span><sup about=\"#mwt18\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-4\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-4\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwHA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwHQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwHg\">[</span>d<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwHw\">]</span></span></a></sup></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr/>\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr><td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b>Incumbent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speaker_of_the_United_States_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Speaker of the United States House of Representatives\">speaker</a></b><br/>\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Johnson\" title=\"Mike Johnson\">Mike Johnson</a><br/>\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></p></td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><br/>\n<p>\n<br/></p></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p id=\"mwIA\">The <b id=\"mwIQ\">2026 United States House of Representatives elections</b> are scheduled to be held on Tuesday, November 3, 2026, as part of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_elections\" title=\"2026 United States elections\" id=\"mwIg\">2026 midterm elections</a> during President <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump\" title=\"Donald Trump\" id=\"mwIw\">Donald Trump</a>'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_presidency_of_Donald_Trump\" title=\"Second presidency of Donald Trump\" id=\"mwJA\">second nonconsecutive term</a>. Voters will elect representatives from all 435 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_congressional_districts\" title=\"List of United States congressional districts\" id=\"mwJQ\">congressional districts</a> across each of the fifty <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._state\" title=\"U.S. state\" id=\"mwJg\">U.S. states</a>, and five of the six <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-voting_members_of_the_United_States_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Non-voting members of the United States House of Representatives\" id=\"mwJw\">non-voting delegates</a> from the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington,_D.C.\" title=\"Washington, D.C.\" id=\"mwKA\">District of Columbia</a> and the inhabited <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insular_area\" title=\"Insular area\" id=\"mwKQ\">U.S. territories</a>.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwKg\">Special elections are also being held on dates throughout 2026. Numerous other federal, state, and local elections, including <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_Senate_elections\" title=\"2026 United States Senate elections\" id=\"mwKw\">elections to the Senate</a>, will be held on this date. The winners of this election will serve in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/120th_United_States_Congress\" title=\"120th United States Congress\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwLA\">120th United States Congress</a>, with seats apportioned among the states based on the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_census\" title=\"2020 United States census\" id=\"mwLQ\">2020 United States census</a> and revised district maps as a result of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025–2026_United_States_redistricting\" title=\"2025–2026 United States redistricting\" id=\"mwLg\">2025–2026 United States redistricting</a>.</p>\n\n<p id=\"mwLw\">Primary elections for all 435 House seats, and five of the six non-voting delegate seats were held starting on March 3, and concluded on September 15, 2026.</p>\n\n<meta property=\"mw:PageProp/toc\" id=\"mwMA\" data-mw='{\"autoGenerated\":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"1\" id=\"mwMQ\" aria-labelledby=\"Retirements\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Retirements\">Retirements</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Retirements\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"2\" id=\"mwMg\" aria-labelledby=\"Summary\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Summary\">Summary</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Summary\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<!--Eleanor Holmes Norton is NOT a representative and should not be counted as such. That is why the sentence is \"(total retirements minus 1) representatives and one non&#x2D;voting delegate\".-->\n<p id=\"mwMw\">60 representatives and two non-voting delegates (26 Democrats and 36 Republicans) have announced their retirement, 29 of whom (9 Democrats and 20 Republicans) are retiring to run for other offices. This is the second-most retirements of representatives in a single election cycle in US history next to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1992_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections\" title=\"1992 United States House of Representatives elections\" id=\"mwNA\">1992</a>, which saw 65 total retirements.<sup about=\"#mwt22\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-5\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-5\" id=\"mwNQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwNg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwNw\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwOA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"3\" id=\"mwOQ\" aria-labelledby=\"Democratic\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Democratic\">Democratic</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Democratic\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt23\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwOg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"div col\",\"href\":\"./Template:Div_col\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}},\"\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"CA\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"11\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":1}},\": [[Nancy Pelosi]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=\\\"Pelosi\\\">{{cite web |last1=Rector |first1=Kevin |title=Rep. Nancy Pelosi, trailblazing Democratic leader from San Francisco, won&apos;t seek reelection |url=https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2025-11-06/rep-nancy-pelosi-former-house-speaker-wont-seek-another-term-in-2026 |access-date=November 6, 2025 |work=[[Los Angeles Times]] |date=November 6, 2025}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"CA\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"26\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":2}},\": [[Julia Brownley]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=\\\"Brownley\\\">{{cite web |url=https://www.vcstar.com/story/news/local/2026/01/08/u-s-rep-julia-brownley-will-not-seek-eighth-term-in-congress/88087843007/|title=\\nU.S. Rep. Julia Brownley announces she will not seek re-election|last1=Huey |first1=Makena|work=[[Ventura County Star]]|date=January 8, 2026|access-date=January 8, 2026}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"DC\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"AL\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":3}},\": [[Eleanor Holmes Norton]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=\\\"HolmesNorton\\\">{{cite web |last=Wu|first=Nicholas|work=[[Politico]]|title=Eleanor Holmes Norton won&apos;t seek reelection as DC delegate|date=January 25, 2026|url=https://www.politico.com/news/2026/01/25/eleanor-holmes-norton-retires-dc-delegate-00731986?cid=apn}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"FL\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"24\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":4}},\": [[Frederica Wilson]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=Wilson>{{cite web|last=Lillis|first=Mike|title=Florida Democrat Frederica Wilson to retire from the House|url=https://thehill.com/homenews/house/5901250-frederica-wilson-retirement-florida/|work=The Hill|date=May 29, 2026|access-date=May 29, 2026}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"GA\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"13\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":5}},\": [[Everton Blair]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=Blair>{{Cite web |last=Kallis |first=Sarah |date=2026-08-26 |title=Everton Blair wins 13th District special election runoff |url=https://www.gpb.org/news/2026/08/26/everton-blair-wins-13th-district-special-election-runoff |access-date=2026-09-06 |website=GPB |quote=November&apos;s general election will decide who represents the district for the next term, starting in January. Blair is not in that race...}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"IL\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":6}},\": [[Robin Kelly]] is retiring to [[2026 United States Senate election in Illinois|run for the U.S. Senate]].&lt;ref name=\\\"Robin\\\">{{cite web |last=Petrella|first=Dan|work=[[Chicago Tribune]]|title=US Rep. Robin Kelly jumps into US Senate race to replace retiring Dick Durbin|date=May 6, 2025|url=https://www.chicagotribune.com/2025/05/06/robin-kelly-running-for-senate/}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"IL\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"4\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":7}},\": [[Chuy García]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=\\\"Garcia\\\">{{cite web |last=Sfondeles|first=Tina|publisher=[[Chicago Public Media]]|title=U.S. Rep Jesus &apos;Chuy&apos; Garcia won&apos;t seek reelection, leaves seat for chief of staff|date=November 3, 2025|url=https://chicago.suntimes.com/elections/2025/11/03/jesus-chuy-garcia-reelection-dropping-out-chief-of-staff-running}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"IL\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"7\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":8}},\": [[Danny Davis (Illinois politician)|Danny Davis]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=\\\"DannyDavis\\\">{{cite web |last=Pearson |first=Rick |date=2025-07-31 |title=US Rep. Danny Davis not running for reelection, backs state Rep. La Shawn Ford as his successor in Congress |url=https://www.chicagotribune.com/2025/07/31/danny-davis-2026-election/ |access-date=2025-07-31 |website=[[The Chicago Tribune]]}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"IL\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"8\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":9}},\": [[Raja Krishnamoorthi]] is retiring to [[2026 United States Senate election in Illinois|run for the U.S. Senate]].&lt;ref name=\\\"Raja\\\">{{cite web |last=Lesniewski |first=Niels |date=2025-05-07 |title=Krishnamoorthi joins Illinois Senate race |url=https://rollcall.com/2025/05/07/krishnamoorthi-joins-illinois-senate-race/ |access-date=2025-05-07 |website=[[Roll Call]] |language=en-US}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"IL\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"9\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":10}},\": [[Jan Schakowsky]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=Schakowsky>{{cite web |last=Sfondeles|first=Tina|title=Rep. Jan Schakowsky announces she won&apos;t seek re-election to congress|url=https://chicago.suntimes.com/2025/05/05/rep-jan-schakowsky-announces-she-wont-seek-re-election-to-congress|date=May 5, 2025|work=[[Chicago Sun-Times]]}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"LA\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"6\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":11}},\": [[Cleo Fields]] is retiring to run for [[2026 United States state legislative elections#Louisiana|Louisiana State Senate]] due to redistricting.&lt;ref name=Fields>{{Cite web |last=Ballard |first=Mark |date=2026-07-21 |title=U.S. Rep. Cleo Fields won&apos;t run for re-election after redistricting. See his next move. |url=https://www.shreveportbossieradvocate.com/news/state_politics/cleo-fields-congress-legislature-reelection/article_2a58d48c-3e2b-54a7-8b04-cb28c91c6fe5.html |access-date=2026-07-21 |website=The Shreveport-Bossier City Advocate |language=en}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"ME\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":12}},\": [[Jared Golden]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=GoldenME>{{cite web |last1=Howard |first1=Andrew |title=Battleground Rep. Jared Golden will not seek reelection |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2025/11/05/jared-golden-retire-2026-election-00638182 |access-date=November 5, 2025 |work=[[Politico]] |date=November 5, 2025 |language=en}}&lt;/ref>\\n#\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"MD\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"5\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":13}},\": [[Steny Hoyer]] is retiring.&lt;ref name=HoyerMD>{{cite web |last1=Karni |first1=Annie |title=Steny Hoyer, Longest-Serving House Democrat, to Retire From Congress |url=https://www.n