}},{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"legend\",\"href\":\"./Template:Legend\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"#808080\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Voluntary redistricting rejected\"}},\"i\":3}},{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"col-2\",\"href\":\"./Template:Col-2\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":4}},{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"legend\",\"href\":\"./Template:Legend\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"#C90000\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Court-ordered/mandatory redistricting\"}},\"i\":5}},{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"legend\",\"href\":\"./Template:Legend\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"#b0b0b0\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Redistricting challenge rejected\"}},\"i\":6}},\"\\n\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"legend\",\"href\":\"./Template:Legend\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"#000000\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"New map finalized; later struck down in court\"}},\"i\":7}},{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"col-end\",\"href\":\"./Template:Col-end\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":8}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1216972533\" about=\"#mwt620\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Col-begin/styles.css\"}}'/></span><div about=\"#mwt619\" id=\"mwBHI\">\n<table class=\" col-begin \" role=\"presentation\"> \n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"col-break col-break-2\"><span class=\"mw-empty-elt\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r981673959\" about=\"#mwt623\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Legend/styles.css\"}}'/></span><div class=\"legend\"><span class=\"legend-color mw-no-invert\" style=\"background-color:#F0F000; color:black;-webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Voluntary redistricting enacted</div><span class=\"mw-empty-elt\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r981673959\" about=\"#mwt625\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Legend/styles.css\"}}'/></span><div class=\"legend\"><span class=\"legend-color mw-no-invert\" style=\"background-color:#808080; color:black;-webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Voluntary redistricting rejected</div></td>\n<td class=\"col-break col-break-2\"><span class=\"mw-empty-elt\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r981673959\" about=\"#mwt628\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Legend/styles.css\"}}'/></span><div class=\"legend\"><span class=\"legend-color mw-no-invert\" style=\"background-color:#C90000; color:white;-webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Court-ordered/mandatory redistricting</div><span class=\"mw-empty-elt\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r981673959\" about=\"#mwt630\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Legend/styles.css\"}}'/></span><div class=\"legend\"><span class=\"legend-color mw-no-invert\" style=\"background-color:#b0b0b0; color:black;-webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>Redistricting challenge rejected</div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r981673959\" about=\"#mwt632\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Legend/styles.css\"}}'/></span><div class=\"legend\"><span class=\"legend-color mw-no-invert\" style=\"background-color:#000000; color:white;-webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact;\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></span><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>New map finalized; later struck down in court</div><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div></figcaption></figure>\n<p id=\"mwBHM\">In the United States, all states with multiple congressional districts are required to revise their district maps following each decennial census to account for population changes. In 2026, most states will use the same districts created in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_redistricting_cycle\" title=\"2020 United States redistricting cycle\" id=\"mwBHQ\">redistricting cycle following the 2020 census</a>, which were first used in the 2022 elections. Maps have changed or would change in several states, often due to legal challenges made based on partisan or racial <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerrymandering_in_the_United_States\" title=\"Gerrymandering in the United States\" id=\"mwBHU\">gerrymandering</a>.<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt634\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBHY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Table alignment\",\"href\":\"./Template:Table_alignment\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1349610755\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" about=\"#mwt635\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Template:Table alignment/styles.css\"}}'>.mw-parser-output .defaultleft,.mw-parser-output .col1left td:nth-child(1),.mw-parser-output .col2left td:nth-child(2),.mw-parser-output .col3left td:nth-child(3),.mw-parser-output .col4left td:nth-child(4),.mw-parser-output .col5left td:nth-child(5),.mw-parser-output .col6left td:nth-child(6),.mw-parser-output .col7left td:nth-child(7),.mw-parser-output .col8left td:nth-child(8),.mw-parser-output .col9left td:nth-child(9),.mw-parser-output .col10left td:nth-child(10),.mw-parser-output .col11left td:nth-child(11),.mw-parser-output .col12left td:nth-child(12),.mw-parser-output .col13left td:nth-child(13),.mw-parser-output .col14left td:nth-child(14),.mw-parser-output .col15left td:nth-child(15),.mw-parser-output .col16left td:nth-child(16),.mw-parser-output .col17left td:nth-child(17),.mw-parser-output .col18left td:nth-child(18),.mw-parser-output .col19left td:nth-child(19),.mw-parser-output .col20left td:nth-child(20),.mw-parser-output .col21left td:nth-child(21),.mw-parser-output .col22left td:nth-child(22),.mw-parser-output .col23left td:nth-child(23),.mw-parser-output .col24left td:nth-child(24),.mw-parser-output .col25left td:nth-child(25),.mw-parser-output .col26left td:nth-child(26),.mw-parser-output .col27left td:nth-child(27),.mw-parser-output .col28left td:nth-child(28),.mw-parser-output .col29left td:nth-child(29),.mw-parser-output .col-1left td:nth-last-child(1),.mw-parser-output .col-2left td:nth-last-child(2),.mw-parser-output .col-3left td:nth-last-child(3),.mw-parser-output .col-4left td:nth-last-child(4),.mw-parser-output .col-5left td:nth-last-child(5),.mw-parser-output .col-6left td:nth-last-child(6),.mw-parser-output .col-7left td:nth-last-child(7),.mw-parser-output .col-8left td:nth-last-child(8),.mw-parser-output .col-9left td:nth-last-child(9){text-align:left}.mw-parser-output .defaultcenter,.mw-parser-output .col1center td:nth-child(1),.mw-parser-output .col2center td:nth-child(2),.mw-parser-output .col3center td:nth-child(3),.mw-parser-output .col4center td:nth-child(4),.mw-parser-output .col5center td:nth-child(5),.mw-parser-output .col6center td:nth-child(6),.mw-parser-output .col7center td:nth-child(7),.mw-parser-output .col8center td:nth-child(8),.mw-parser-output .col9center td:nth-child(9),.mw-parser-output .col10center td:nth-child(10),.mw-parser-output .col11center td:nth-child(11),.mw-parser-output .col12center td:nth-child(12),.mw-parser-output .col13center td:nth-child(13),.mw-parser-output .col14center td:nth-child(14),.mw-parser-output .col15center td:nth-child(15),.mw-parser-output .col16center td:nth-child(16),.mw-parser-output .col17center td:nth-child(17),.mw-parser-output .col18center td:nth-child(18),.mw-parser-output .col19center td:nth-child(19),.mw-parser-output .col20center td:nth-child(20),.mw-parser-output .col21center td:nth-child(21),.mw-parser-output .col22center td:nth-child(22),.mw-parser-output .col23center td:nth-child(23),.mw-parser-output .col24center td:nth-child(24),.mw-parser-output .col25center td:nth-child(25),.mw-parser-output .col26center td:nth-child(26),.mw-parser-output .col27center td:nth-child(27),.mw-parser-output .col28center td:nth-child(28),.mw-parser-output .col29center td:nth-child(29),.mw-parser-output .col-1center td:nth-last-child(1),.mw-parser-output .col-2center td:nth-last-child(2),.mw-parser-output .col-3center td:nth-last-child(3),.mw-parser-output .col-4center td:nth-last-child(4),.mw-parser-output .col-5center td:nth-last-child(5),.mw-parser-output .col-6center td:nth-last-child(6),.mw-parser-output .col-7center td:nth-last-child(7),.mw-parser-output .col-8center td:nth-last-child(8),.mw-parser-output .col-9center td:nth-last-child(9){text-align:center}.mw-parser-output .defaultright,.mw-parser-output .col1right td:nth-child(1),.mw-parser-output .col2right td:nth-child(2),.mw-parser-output .col3right td:nth-child(3),.mw-parser-output .col4right td:nth-child(4),.mw-parser-output .col5right td:nth-child(5),.mw-parser-output .col6right td:nth-child(6),.mw-parser-output .col7right td:nth-child(7),.mw-parser-output .col8right td:nth-child(8),.mw-parser-output .col9right td:nth-child(9),.mw-parser-output .col10right td:nth-child(10),.mw-parser-output .col11right td:nth-child(11),.mw-parser-output .col12right td:nth-child(12),.mw-parser-output .col13right td:nth-child(13),.mw-parser-output .col14right td:nth-child(14),.mw-parser-output .col15right td:nth-child(15),.mw-parser-output .col16right td:nth-child(16),.mw-parser-output .col17right td:nth-child(17),.mw-parser-output .col18right td:nth-child(18),.mw-parser-output .col19right td:nth-child(19),.mw-parser-output .col20right td:nth-child(20),.mw-parser-output .col21right td:nth-child(21),.mw-parser-output .col22right td:nth-child(22),.mw-parser-output .col23right td:nth-child(23),.mw-parser-output .col24right td:nth-child(24),.mw-parser-output .col25right td:nth-child(25),.mw-parser-output .col26right td:nth-child(26),.mw-parser-output .col27right td:nth-child(27),.mw-parser-output .col28right td:nth-child(28),.mw-parser-output .col29right td:nth-child(29),.mw-parser-output .col-1right td:nth-last-child(1),.mw-parser-output .col-2right td:nth-last-child(2),.mw-parser-output .col-3right td:nth-last-child(3),.mw-parser-output .col-4right td:nth-last-child(4),.mw-parser-output .col-5right td:nth-last-child(5),.mw-parser-output .col-6right td:nth-last-child(6),.mw-parser-output .col-7right td:nth-last-child(7),.mw-parser-output .col-8right td:nth-last-child(8),.mw-parser-output .col-9right td:nth-last-child(9){text-align:right}</style></span></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwBHc\">As of <span about=\"#mwt636\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBHg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"monthyear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Monthyear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'>October 2026</span>, several states have seen challenges to their <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_United_States_congressional_districts\" title=\"List of United States congressional districts\" id=\"mwBHk\">congressional district</a> maps that were put in place during the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_United_States_redistricting_cycle\" title=\"2020 United States redistricting cycle\" id=\"mwBHo\">redistricting cycle</a> brought upon by the results of the 2020 census. In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Arkansas\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Arkansas\" id=\"mwBHs\">Arkansas</a>, a federal court dismissed a case against their congressional map that argued the map did not comply with the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voting_Rights_Act\" title=\"Voting Rights Act\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBHw\">Voting Rights Act</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt639\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-99\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-99\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-99\" id=\"mwBH0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBH4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBH8\">[</span>89<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIA\">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_Florida\" title=\"Supreme Court of Florida\" id=\"mwBIE\">Florida Supreme Court</a> dismissed a challenge regarding the Florida's congressional map, finding a new plurality-Black congressional district would be against federal law.<sup about=\"#mwt642\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-100\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-100\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-100\" id=\"mwBII\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBIM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIQ\">[</span>90<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwBIY\">In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Georgia\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Georgia\" id=\"mwBIc\">Georgia</a>, litigation is still ongoing regarding appeals to the newly drawn congressional map that was used in the 2024 elections. However, it was not resolved before the filing deadline for the 2026 Congressional elections.<sup about=\"#mwt645\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-101\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-101\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-101\" id=\"mwBIg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBIk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIo\">[</span>91<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIs\">]</span></span></a></sup> In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Louisiana\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Louisiana\" id=\"mwBIw\">Louisiana</a>, litigation remained unresolved.<sup about=\"#mwt648\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-SC_102-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"SC\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-SC-102\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-SC-102\" id=\"mwBI0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBI4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBI8\">[</span>92<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBJA\">]</span></span></a></sup> In South Carolina, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Carolina_Supreme_Court\" title=\"South Carolina Supreme Court\" id=\"mwBJE\">South Carolina Supreme Court</a> ruled that partisan gerrymandering is not in violation of the state's constitution, keeping the maps in place.<sup about=\"#mwt651\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:0_103-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":0\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-103\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:0-103\" id=\"mwBJI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBJM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBJQ\">[</span>93<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBJU\">]</span></span></a></sup> In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas\" title=\"Texas\" id=\"mwBJY\">Texas</a>, a trial was held in federal court in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Paso,_Texas\" title=\"El Paso, Texas\" id=\"mwBJc\">El Paso</a> to determine whether its congressional map discriminated against Black and Latino voters in violation of the VRA,<sup about=\"#mwt654\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TXmap1_104-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"TXmap1\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-TXmap1-104\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-TXmap1-104\" id=\"mwBJg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBJk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBJo\">[</span>94<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBJs\">]</span></span></a></sup> but the case was paused pending expected new maps in the state.<sup about=\"#mwt657\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-LULAC_105-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"LULAC\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-LULAC-105\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-LULAC-105\" id=\"mwBJw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBJ0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBJ4\">[</span>95<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBJ8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwBKA\">In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Utah\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Utah\" id=\"mwBKE\">Utah</a>, a partisan gerrymander case resulted in a map which creates a safe Democratic district comprising the majority of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_Lake_County\" title=\"Salt Lake County\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBKI\">Salt Lake County</a> following a district court ruling.<sup about=\"#mwt660\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:4_106-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":4\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:4-106\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:4-106\" id=\"mwBKM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBKQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBKU\">[</span>96<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBKY\">]</span></span></a></sup> In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Wisconsin\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Wisconsin\" id=\"mwBKc\">Wisconsin</a>, a challenge to the state's current congressional map, arguing it was an unlawful partisan gerrymander, was dismissed by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wisconsin_Supreme_Court\" title=\"Wisconsin Supreme Court\" id=\"mwBKg\">Wisconsin Supreme Court</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt663\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-autogenerated3_107-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"autogenerated3\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-autogenerated3-107\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-autogenerated3-107\" id=\"mwBKk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBKo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBKs\">[</span>97<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBKw\">]</span></span></a></sup> A new map was required in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Ohio\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Ohio\" id=\"mwBK0\">Ohio</a> due to the Congressional Redistricting Procedures Amendment to Section XI of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Ohio\" title=\"Constitution of Ohio\" id=\"mwBK4\">state's constitution</a>, resulting in two districts becoming more Republican leaning.<sup about=\"#mwt664\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-OHnewmap_108-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"OHnewmap\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-OHnewmap-108\" id=\"mwBK8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBLA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBLE\">[</span>98<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBLI\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"19\" id=\"mwBLM\" aria-labelledby=\"Out-of-cycle_partisan_redistricting_efforts\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Out-of-cycle_partisan_redistricting_efforts\">Out-of-cycle partisan redistricting efforts</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Out-of-cycle partisan redistricting efforts\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p id=\"mwBLQ\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Abbott\" title=\"Greg Abbott\" id=\"mwBLU\">Governor Greg Abbott</a> called a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special_session\" title=\"Special session\" id=\"mwBLY\">special session</a> of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas_Legislature\" title=\"Texas Legislature\" id=\"mwBLc\">Texas Legislature</a> to redraw its congressional districts, leading to the Texas Legislature passing new maps resulting in 5 new Republican-leaning districts.<sup about=\"#mwt667\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-tg_109-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"tg\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-tg-109\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-tg-109\" id=\"mwBLg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBLk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBLo\">[</span>99<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBLs\">]</span></span></a></sup> On November 18, a panel of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_District_Court_for_the_Western_District_of_Texas\" title=\"United States District Court for the Western District of Texas\" id=\"mwBLw\">District Court for the Western District of Texas</a> issued a preliminary injunction blocking the new map, putting the former map back in place,<sup about=\"#mwt670\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:5_110-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":5\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:5-110\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:5-110\" id=\"mwBL0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBL4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBL8\">[</span>100<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBMA\">]</span></span></a></sup> but the Supreme Court later placed an administrative stay on the ruling, allowing the new maps to stand.<sup about=\"#mwt673\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TXmap_111-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"TXmap\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-TXmap-111\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-TXmap-111\" id=\"mwBME\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBMI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBMM\">[</span>101<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBMQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_DeSantis\" title=\"Ron DeSantis\" id=\"mwBMU\">Governor Ron DeSantis</a> has expressed interest in redrawing <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Florida\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Florida\" id=\"mwBMY\">Florida's</a> congressional map, and the Florida House has created a special redistricting committee.<sup about=\"#mwt676\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-112\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-112\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-112\" id=\"mwBMc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBMg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBMk\">[</span>102<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBMo\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Kehoe\" title=\"Mike Kehoe\" id=\"mwBMs\">Governor Mike Kehoe</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Missouri\" title=\"Missouri\" id=\"mwBMw\">Missouri</a> called a special session on August 29, 2025, which redrew the solid Democratic <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Missouri's_5th_congressional_district\" title=\"Missouri's 5th congressional district\" id=\"mwBM0\">5th district</a> to a solid Republican district, allowing the GOP to pick up a seat.<sup about=\"#mwt679\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:1_113-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":1\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-113\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:1-113\" id=\"mwBM4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBM8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNA\">[</span>103<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNE\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, on September 3, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Missouri_Supreme_Court\" title=\"Missouri Supreme Court\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBNI\">Missouri Supreme Court</a> unanimously ruled that the referendum on the new maps was sufficient and must be put on the ballot, thus leaving the 2022 maps in place for the 2026 elections.<sup about=\"#mwt682\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:6_114-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":6\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:6-114\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:6-114\" id=\"mwBNM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBNQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNU\">[</span>104<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNY\">]</span></span></a></sup> Republican state legislative leaders in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_North_Carolina\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in North Carolina\" id=\"mwBNc\">North Carolina</a> announced a redraw of the state's congressional districts to make the 1st congressional district more Republican leaning.<sup about=\"#mwt683\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-NCmap_115-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"NCmap\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-NCmap-115\" id=\"mwBNg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBNk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNo\">[</span>105<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwBNw\">Talks and efforts about redistricting occurred in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Nebraska\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Nebraska\" id=\"mwBN0\">Nebraska</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_New_Hampshire\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in New Hampshire\" id=\"mwBN4\">New Hampshire</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Indiana\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Indiana\" id=\"mwBN8\">Indiana</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Kansas\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Kansas\" id=\"mwBOA\">Kansas</a>, but either failed or did not gain traction.<sup about=\"#mwt686\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-116\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-116\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-116\" id=\"mwBOE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBOI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOM\">[</span>106<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOQ\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt689\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-117\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-117\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-117\" id=\"mwBOU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBOY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOc\">[</span>107<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOg\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt690\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-INmap_118-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"INmap\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-INmap-118\" id=\"mwBOk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBOo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOs\">[</span>108<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOw\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt691\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-KSmap_119-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"KSmap\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-KSmap-119\" id=\"mwBO0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBO4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBO8\">[</span>109<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBPA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwBPE\">Democrats have threatened to retaliate against attempts to mid-decade redistrict for partisan gain and have stated the possibility of redrawing the congressional maps in blue states. In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_California\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in California\" id=\"mwBPI\">California</a>, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_State_Legislature\" title=\"California State Legislature\" id=\"mwBPM\">state legislature</a> drafted a map eliminating five Republican districts to combat Texas's plan, which was approved by voters. In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Virginia\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Virginia\" id=\"mwBPQ\">Virginia</a>, members of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_General_Assembly\" title=\"Virginia General Assembly\" id=\"mwBPU\">General Assembly</a> announced a plan on October 23, 2025 to begin the process to redraw the state's congressional districts before the 2026 elections.<sup about=\"#mwt694\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-auto_120-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"auto\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-auto-120\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-auto-120\" id=\"mwBPY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBPc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBPg\">[</span>110<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBPk\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n\n<p id=\"mwBPo\">Democratic governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wes_Moore\" title=\"Wes Moore\" id=\"mwBPs\">Wes Moore</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Maryland\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Maryland\" id=\"mwBPw\">Maryland</a> unsuccessfully pursued redistricting in his state.<sup about=\"#mwt695\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-MDmap_121-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"MDmap\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-MDmap-121\" id=\"mwBP0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBP4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBP8\">[</span>111<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQA\">]</span></span></a></sup> Redistricting has been considered in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Colorado\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in Colorado\" id=\"mwBQE\">Colorado</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_New_Jersey\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in New Jersey\" id=\"mwBQI\">New Jersey</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_New_York\" title=\"2026 United States House of Representatives elections in New York\" id=\"mwBQM\">New York</a>. Legal and political challenges make redistricting before 2026 highly unlikely.<sup about=\"#mwt698\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-122\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-122\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-122\" id=\"mwBQQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBQU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQY\">[</span>112<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQc\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt701\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-123\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-123\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-123\" id=\"mwBQg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBQk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQo\">[</span>113<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQs\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt704\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-124\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-124\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-124\" id=\"mwBQw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBQ0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQ4\">[</span>114<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQ8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt705\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBRA\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable defaultleft col4center col5center col6center col7center\" id=\"mwBRE\">\n<caption id=\"mwBRI\">Summary of mid-decade changes to congressional districts in advance of the 2026 election cycle</caption>\n<tbody id=\"mwBRM\"><tr id=\"mwBRQ\"><th rowspan=\"2\" id=\"mwBRU\">State<br id=\"mwBRY\"/><span style=\"font-size: 85%;\" about=\"#mwt706\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBRc\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Small\",\"href\":\"./Template:Small\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"(linked to&lt;br>summaries below)\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>(linked to<br/>summaries below)</span></th>\n<th rowspan=\"2\" id=\"mwBRg\">Status</th>\n<th rowspan=\"2\" class=\"unsortable\" id=\"mwBRk\">Notes</th>\n<th colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center\" id=\"mwBRo\">Change in partisanship<sup about=\"#mwt707\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-change_125-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"change\",\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-change-125\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"efn \",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Competitive seats are defined as seats won by less than 10 points by their respective party in 2024\"},\"name\":{\"wt\":\"change\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a href=\"#cite_note-change-125\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwBRs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBRw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBR0\">[</span>k<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBR4\">]</span></span></a></sup></th></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBR8\">\n<th id=\"mwBSA\"><abbr title=\"Democratic-leaning seats\" about=\"#mwt710\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:ExpandedAttrs\" id=\"mwBSI\" data-mw='{\"attribs\":[[{\"txt\":\"title\"},{\"html\":\"&lt;span typeof=\\\"mw:Nowiki\\\" id=\\\"mwBSE\\\">Democratic-leaning seats&lt;/span>\"}]],\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Abbr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Abbr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"D\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Democratic-leaning seats\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>D</abbr></th>\n<th id=\"mwBSM\"><abbr title=\"Highly competitive seats\" about=\"#mwt712\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:ExpandedAttrs\" id=\"mwBSU\" data-mw='{\"attribs\":[[{\"txt\":\"title\"},{\"html\":\"&lt;span typeof=\\\"mw:Nowiki\\\" id=\\\"mwBSQ\\\">Highly competitive seats&lt;/span>\"}]],\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Abbr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Abbr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"C\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Highly competitive seats\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>C</abbr></th>\n<th id=\"mwBSY\"><abbr title=\"Republican-leaning seats\" about=\"#mwt714\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:ExpandedAttrs\" id=\"mwBSg\" data-mw='{\"attribs\":[[{\"txt\":\"title\"},{\"html\":\"&lt;span typeof=\\\"mw:Nowiki\\\" id=\\\"mwBSc\\\">Republican-leaning seats&lt;/span>\"}]],\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Abbr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Abbr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"R\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Republican-leaning seats\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>R</abbr></th></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBSk\">\n<th id=\"mwBSo\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Alabama\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBSs\">Alabama</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Yes\" style=\"background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-yes2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt716\" id=\"mwBSw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=0 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ya\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ya\"},\"params\":{\"text\":{\"wt\":\"New districts enacted\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>New districts enacted</td>\n<td id=\"mwBS0\">In April 2026, the Supreme Court ruled on <i id=\"mwBS4\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_v._Callais\" title=\"Louisiana v. Callais\" id=\"mwBS8\">Louisiana v. Callais</a></i> that stricter scrutiny had to be applied with regard to section 2 of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voting_Rights_Act\" title=\"Voting Rights Act\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBTA\">Voting Rights Act</a>. Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kay_Ivey\" title=\"Kay Ivey\" id=\"mwBTE\">Kay Ivey</a> was initially reluctant to call a special session after <i id=\"mwBTI\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allen_v._Milligan\" title=\"Allen v. Milligan\" id=\"mwBTM\">Allen v. Milligan</a></i>, but was lobbied to do so by the state attorney general and secretary of state, both of whom also filed emergency injunctions to lift the requirements levied on them by the federal courts.<sup about=\"#mwt720\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-126\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-126\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-126\" id=\"mwBTQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBTU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBTY\">[</span>115<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBTc\">]</span></span></a></sup> <div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt717\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBTg\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>The Supreme Court voted 6–3 to lift the stay, paving the way for state legislators to redraw.<sup about=\"#mwt723\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-127\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-127\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-127\" id=\"mwBTk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBTo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBTs\">[</span>116<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBTw\">]</span></span></a></sup> On May 26, 2026, an Alabama court blocked the new map, arguing that the <i id=\"mwBT0\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_v._Callais\" title=\"Louisiana v. Callais\" id=\"mwBT4\">Louisiana v. Callais</a></i> decision does not change the fact that the map intentionally discriminates against African-American voters in violation of the Constitution.<sup about=\"#mwt726\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-128\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-128\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-128\" id=\"mwBT8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBUA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBUE\">[</span>117<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBUI\">]</span></span></a></sup> On June 2, 2026, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_the_United_States\" title=\"Supreme Court of the United States\" id=\"mwBUM\">Supreme Court</a> granted stay on the block, allowing the new map to be implemented.<sup about=\"#mwt729\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-129\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-129\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-129\" id=\"mwBUQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBUU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBUY\">[</span>118<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBUc\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td id=\"mwBUg\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt730\" id=\"mwBUk\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"steady\",\"href\":\"./Template:Steady\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td id=\"mwBUo\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt731\" id=\"mwBUs\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td>\n<td id=\"mwBUw\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt732\" id=\"mwBU0\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBU4\">\n<th id=\"mwBU8\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Arkansas\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBVA\">Arkansas</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"3\" style=\"background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-no2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt733\" id=\"mwBVE\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=3 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"no2\",\"href\":\"./Template:No2\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Districts left in place\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>Districts left in place</td>\n<td id=\"mwBVI\">In <i id=\"mwBVM\">Christian Ministerial Alliance v. Thurston</i>, plaintiffs alleged racial gerrymandering diluting the voting power of black voters by splitting <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Rock\" title=\"Little Rock\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBVQ\">Little Rock</a> into three districts. The case was heard in a federal district court. The panel ruled that it did not constitute a racial gerrymander and dismissed the case.<sup about=\"#mwt736\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-130\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-130\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-130\" id=\"mwBVU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBVY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBVc\">[</span>119<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBVg\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwBVk\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt737\" id=\"mwBVo\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwBVs\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt738\" id=\"mwBVw\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwBV0\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt739\" id=\"mwBV4\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBV8\">\n<th id=\"mwBWA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#California\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBWE\">California</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Yes\" style=\"background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-yes2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt740\" id=\"mwBWI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=0 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ya\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ya\"},\"params\":{\"text\":{\"wt\":\"[[2025 California proposed redistricting|New districts enacted]]\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_California_proposed_redistricting\" title=\"2025 California proposed redistricting\" class=\"mw-redirect\">New districts enacted</a></td>\n<td id=\"mwBWM\">In response to Texas's redistricting, a new map was approved by voters in a special statewide election temporarily permitting an off-cycle redistricting. The state's <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_California\" title=\"Constitution of California\" id=\"mwBWQ\">constitution</a> prohibits the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California_State_Legislature\" title=\"California State Legislature\" id=\"mwBWU\">state legislature</a> from drawing congressional districts, so the map was subject to a 2025 referendum. It was passed by two-thirds of the legislature and over a 64% majority approval by the state's voters for the new districts to take place.<sup about=\"#mwt743\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CM_131-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"CM\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CM-131\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-CM-131\" id=\"mwBWY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBWc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBWg\">[</span>120<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBWk\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td id=\"mwBWo\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt744\" id=\"mwBWs\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 4</td>\n<td id=\"mwBWw\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt745\" id=\"mwBW0\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 3</td>\n<td id=\"mwBW4\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt746\" id=\"mwBW8\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBXA\">\n<th id=\"mwBXE\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Florida\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBXI\">Florida</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Yes\" style=\"background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-yes2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt747\" id=\"mwBXM\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=0 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ya\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ya\"},\"params\":{\"text\":{\"wt\":\"[[2026 Florida redistricting|New districts enacted]]\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Florida_redistricting\" title=\"2026 Florida redistricting\">New districts enacted</a></td>\n<td id=\"mwBXQ\">In September 2023, a state circuit judge ruled that the map passed by the state legislature discriminated against Black voters, by redrawing the formerly plurality-Black 5th district to no longer have a Black plurality. Florida appealed this ruling and the map was reinstated by an appeals court.<sup about=\"#mwt751\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-132\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-132\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-132\" id=\"mwBXU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBXY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBXc\">[</span>121<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBXg\">]</span></span></a></sup><wbr id=\"mwBXk\"/> In July 2025, the Florida Supreme Court ruled 5–1 to keep the current maps in place, finding that creating a plurality-Black congressional district would violate the federal <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equal_Protection_Clause\" title=\"Equal Protection Clause\" id=\"mwBXo\">Equal Protection Clause</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt754\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-133\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-133\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-133\" id=\"mwBXs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBXw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBX0\">[</span>122<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBX4\">]</span></span></a></sup><div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt748\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBX8\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>On January 9, 2026, Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_DeSantis\" title=\"Ron DeSantis\" id=\"mwBYA\">Ron DeSantis</a> called for a special session in April redrawing the state's congressional maps with the target of gaining 3 to 5 new Republican seats. However, Florida state law prevents deliberately redrawing congressional maps purely for partisan gain.<sup about=\"#mwt757\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-134\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-134\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-134\" id=\"mwBYE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBYI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYM\">[</span>123<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 27, 2026, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_Florida\" title=\"Supreme Court of Florida\" id=\"mwBYU\">Supreme Court of Florida</a> rejected a petition to block the special session.<sup about=\"#mwt760\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-135\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-135\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-135\" id=\"mwBYY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBYc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYg\">[</span>124<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYk\">]</span></span></a></sup> On April 29, 2026, the maps were approved by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florida_Legislature\" title=\"Florida Legislature\" id=\"mwBYo\">Florida Legislature</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt763\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-136\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-136\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-136\" id=\"mwBYs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBYw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBY0\">[</span>125<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBY4\">]</span></span></a></sup> On May 4, 2026, Governor DeSantis signed the new map into law.<sup about=\"#mwt766\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-137\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-137\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-137\" id=\"mwBY8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBZA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBZE\">[</span>126<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBZI\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td id=\"mwBZM\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt767\" id=\"mwBZQ\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td>\n<td id=\"mwBZU\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt768\" id=\"mwBZY\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 4</td>\n<td id=\"mwBZc\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt769\" id=\"mwBZg\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 3</td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBZk\">\n<th id=\"mwBZo\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Indiana\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBZs\">Indiana</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"3\" style=\"background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-no2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt770\" id=\"mwBZw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=3 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"no2\",\"href\":\"./Template:No2\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Districts left in place\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>Districts left in place</td>\n<td id=\"mwBZ0\">On November 18, 2025, the Indiana State Senate voted 29–19 against meeting in December with their House colleagues to discuss redistricting.<sup about=\"#mwt773\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-138\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-138\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-138\" id=\"mwBZ4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBZ8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBaA\">[</span>127<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBaE\">]</span></span></a></sup> Despite this, Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Braun\" title=\"Mike Braun\" id=\"mwBaI\">Mike Braun</a> stated that he would \"explore all options\" to enable redistricting, in response to pressure from President Trump. On November 25, the state senate announced it would vote on a potential proposal approved by the state house.<sup about=\"#mwt776\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-139\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-139\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-139\" id=\"mwBaM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBaQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBaU\">[</span>128<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBaY\">]</span></span></a></sup> After passing in the state house, the state senate rejected the proposal 31–19.<sup about=\"#mwt779\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-INmap_118-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"INmap\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-INmap-118\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-INmap-118\" id=\"mwBac\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBag\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBak\">[</span>108<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBao\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwBas\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt780\" id=\"mwBaw\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwBa0\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt781\" id=\"mwBa4\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwBa8\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt782\" id=\"mwBbA\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBbE\">\n<th id=\"mwBbI\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Kansas\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBbM\">Kansas</a></th>\n<td style=\"background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-no2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt783\" id=\"mwBbQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"no2\",\"href\":\"./Template:No2\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Districts left in place\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>Districts left in place</td>\n<td id=\"mwBbU\">Republican Kansas state legislators announced a plan to call a special session to redraw the 3rd congressional district, but lacked the necessary support in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kansas_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Kansas House of Representatives\" id=\"mwBbY\">House</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt786\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-KSmap_119-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"KSmap\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-KSmap-119\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-KSmap-119\" id=\"mwBbc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBbg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBbk\">[</span>109<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBbo\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwBbs\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt787\" id=\"mwBbw\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwBb0\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt788\" id=\"mwBb4\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwBb8\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt789\" id=\"mwBcA\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBcE\">\n<th id=\"mwBcI\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Louisiana\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBcM\">Louisiana</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Yes\" style=\"background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-yes2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt790\" id=\"mwBcQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=0 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ya\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ya\"},\"params\":{\"text\":{\"wt\":\"New districts enacted\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>New districts enacted</td>\n<td id=\"mwBcU\">In April 2026, the Supreme Court ruled on <i id=\"mwBcY\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_v._Callais\" title=\"Louisiana v. Callais\" id=\"mwBcc\">Louisiana v. Callais</a></i> that stricter scrutiny had to be applied with regard to section 2 of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voting_Rights_Act\" title=\"Voting Rights Act\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBcg\">Voting Rights Act</a>. The state following the ruling requested the Court strike down the lower court ruling to have two black majority districts, which it proceeded to do. The state government has pushed to move back the primary dates in light of the court requiring redistricting.<sup about=\"#mwt793\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-140\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-140\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-140\" id=\"mwBck\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBco\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBcs\">[</span>129<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBcw\">]</span></span></a></sup> On May 29, 2026, Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeff_Landry\" title=\"Jeff Landry\" id=\"mwBc0\">Jeff Landry</a> signed a new map into law, removing one of the two plurality-Black, Democratic-controlled districts.<sup about=\"#mwt796\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-141\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-141\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-141\" id=\"mwBc4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBc8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBdA\">[</span>130<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBdE\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td id=\"mwBdI\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt797\" id=\"mwBdM\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td>\n<td id=\"mwBdQ\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt798\" id=\"mwBdU\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"steady\",\"href\":\"./Template:Steady\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td id=\"mwBdY\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt799\" id=\"mwBdc\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBdg\">\n<th id=\"mwBdk\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Maryland\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBdo\">Maryland</a></th>\n<td style=\"background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-no2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt800\" id=\"mwBds\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"no2\",\"href\":\"./Template:No2\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Districts left in place\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>Districts left in place</td>\n<td id=\"mwBdw\">In November 2025, Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wes_Moore\" title=\"Wes Moore\" id=\"mwBd0\">Wes Moore</a> announced the creation of the Redistricting Advisory Commission which began the process of redistricting the congressional lines to make the 1st district more Democratic. The plan has received support from State House Speaker <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseline_Peña-Melnyk\" title=\"Joseline Peña-Melnyk\" id=\"mwBd4\">Joseline Peña-Melnyk</a>, but opposition from State Senate President <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Ferguson_(politician)\" title=\"Bill Ferguson (politician)\" id=\"mwBd8\">Bill Ferguson</a>. In January 2026, the Governor's Redistricting Advisory Commission voted to recommend a congressional map that would redraw the 1st congressional district to make it more favorable for Democrats.<sup about=\"#mwt803\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-142\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-142\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-142\" id=\"mwBeA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBeE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBeI\">[</span>131<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBeM\">]</span></span></a></sup> The map passed the state house on February 2.<sup about=\"#mwt806\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-MDmap_121-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"MDmap\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MDmap-121\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-MDmap-121\" id=\"mwBeQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBeU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBeY\">[</span>111<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBec\">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 20, Ferguson told reporters that the window to redraw Maryland's congressional maps had closed, killing the bill.<sup about=\"#mwt809\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-143\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-143\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-143\" id=\"mwBeg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBek\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBeo\">[</span>132<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBes\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwBew\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt810\" id=\"mwBe0\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwBe4\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt811\" id=\"mwBe8\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwBfA\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt812\" id=\"mwBfE\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBfI\">\n<th id=\"mwBfM\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Missouri\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBfQ\">Missouri</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"3\" style=\"background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-no2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt813\" id=\"mwBfU\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=3 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"no2\",\"href\":\"./Template:No2\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"[[2025 Missouri redistricting|Districts left in place]]\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Missouri_redistricting\" title=\"2025 Missouri redistricting\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Districts left in place</a></td>\n<td id=\"mwBfY\">The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Missouri_Legislature\" title=\"Missouri Legislature\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBfc\">Missouri Legislature</a> passed maps to create a new safely Republican seat in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Missouri's_5th_congressional_district\" title=\"Missouri's 5th congressional district\" id=\"mwBfg\">5th district</a>. Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Kehoe\" title=\"Mike Kehoe\" id=\"mwBfk\">Mike Kehoe</a> signed the map into law in September 2025.<sup about=\"#mwt814\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:1_113-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":1\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:1-113\" id=\"mwBfo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBfs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBfw\">[</span>103<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBf0\">]</span></span></a></sup> The maps may be blocked by a referendum if enough signatures are gathered.<sup about=\"#mwt817\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-144\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-144\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-144\" id=\"mwBf4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBf8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgA\">[</span>133<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgE\">]</span></span></a></sup> In March 2026, opponents of the map said they had enough signatures for the referendum to qualify.<sup about=\"#mwt820\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Signatures_145-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Signatures\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Signatures-145\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-Signatures-145\" id=\"mwBgI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBgM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgQ\">[</span>134<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgU\">]</span></span></a></sup>\n<p id=\"mwBgY\">On August 4, 2026, Missouri Secretary of State <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denny_Hoskins\" title=\"Denny Hoskins\" id=\"mwBgc\">Denny Hoskins</a> blocked the referendum from taking place, arguing that the referendum would be unconstitutional under <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Missouri\" title=\"Constitution of Missouri\" id=\"mwBgg\">Missouri's Constitution</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt823\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-146\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-146\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-146\" id=\"mwBgk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBgo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgs\">[</span>135<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgw\">]</span></span></a></sup> a decision which was upheld by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cole_County,_Missouri\" title=\"Cole County, Missouri\" id=\"mwBg0\">Cole County</a> Circuit Judge Daniel Green on August 19.<sup about=\"#mwt826\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-147\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-147\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-147\" id=\"mwBg4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBg8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBhA\">[</span>136<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBhE\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, on September 3, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Missouri_Supreme_Court\" title=\"Missouri Supreme Court\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBhI\">Missouri Supreme Court</a> unanimously ruled that the referendum is sufficient and must be put on the ballot, thus leaving the 2022 maps in place for the 2026 elections.<sup about=\"#mwt827\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:6_114-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":6\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:6-114\" id=\"mwBhM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBhQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBhU\">[</span>104<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBhY\">]</span></span></a></sup> On September 8, U.S. Supreme Court Justice <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brett_Kavanaugh\" title=\"Brett Kavanaugh\" id=\"mwBhc\">Brett Kavanaugh</a> denied an emergency appeal by State Republicans.<sup about=\"#mwt830\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-148\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-148\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-148\" id=\"mwBhg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBhk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBho\">[</span>137<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBhs\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt833\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-149\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-149\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-149\" id=\"mwBhw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBh0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBh4\">[</span>138<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBh8\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, the same day, Chief U.S. District Judge <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_R._Clark\" title=\"Stephen R. Clark\" id=\"mwBiA\">Stephen Clark</a> of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_District_Court_for_the_Eastern_District_of_Missouri\" title=\"United States District Court for the Eastern District of Missouri\" id=\"mwBiE\">Eastern District of Missouri</a> issued a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temporary_restraining_order\" title=\"Temporary restraining order\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBiI\">temporary restraining order</a> in a separate lawsuit prohibiting the state from using anything but the new 2025 maps.<sup about=\"#mwt836\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-150\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-150\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-150\" id=\"mwBiM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBiQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBiU\">[</span>139<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBiY\">]</span></span></a></sup> On September 10, the U.S. Supreme Court granted an emergency stay of Judge Clark's order, putting the 2022 map back into place for the 2026 elections.<sup about=\"#mwt839\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-151\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-151\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-151\" id=\"mwBic\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBig\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBik\">[</span>140<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBio\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, on September 21, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Court_of_Appeals_for_the_Eighth_Circuit\" title=\"United States Court of Appeals for the Eighth Circuit\" id=\"mwBis\">United States Court of Appeals for the Eighth Circuit</a>, ruling on the merits, affirmed the temporary restraining order and remanded the case to the lower court for entry of a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Permanent_injunction\" title=\"Permanent injunction\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBiw\">permanent injunction</a> enjoining Missouri to use the 2025 map, but stayed their ruling for a week pending appeal to the U.S. Supreme Court.<sup about=\"#mwt842\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-152\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-152\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-152\" id=\"mwBi0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBi4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBi8\">[</span>141<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBjA\">]</span></span></a></sup> On September 25, the U.S. Supreme Court unanimously held that state law rules in the case and granted an emergency stay of the Eighth Circuit's order and Judge Clark's injunction, leaving the 2022 maps in place for the 2026 elections.<sup about=\"#mwt845\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-153\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-153\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-153\" id=\"mwBjE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBjI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBjM\">[</span>142<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBjQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwBjU\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt846\" id=\"mwBjY\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwBjc\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt847\" id=\"mwBjg\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwBjk\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt848\" id=\"mwBjo\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBjs\">\n<th id=\"mwBjw\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#New_York\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBj0\">New York</a></th>\n<td style=\"background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-no2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt849\" id=\"mwBj4\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"no2\",\"href\":\"./Template:No2\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Districts left in place\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>Districts left in place</td>\n<td id=\"mwBj8\">Voters in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York's_11th_congressional_district\" title=\"New York's 11th congressional district\" id=\"mwBkA\">NY-11</a> filed a lawsuit in October 2025, claiming the Staten Island-based district illegally dilutes the power of Black and Hispanic voters in the district.<sup about=\"#mwt852\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-154\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-154\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-154\" id=\"mwBkE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBkI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBkM\">[</span>143<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBkQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> Acting <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Supreme_Court\" title=\"New York Supreme Court\" id=\"mwBkU\">New York Supreme Court</a> Justice <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeffrey_Pearlman\" title=\"Jeffrey Pearlman\" id=\"mwBkY\">Jeffrey Pearlman</a> ordered the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_redistricting_commission\" title=\"Independent redistricting commission\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBkc\">independent redistricting commission</a> to make new maps to reconfigure NY-11 by February 6, 2026.<sup about=\"#mwt855\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-NYMap_155-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"NYMap\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NYMap-155\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-NYMap-155\" id=\"mwBkg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBkk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBko\">[</span>144<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBks\">]</span></span></a></sup> The deadline was suspended after <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicole_Malliotakis\" title=\"Nicole Malliotakis\" id=\"mwBkw\">Rep. Malliotakis</a>, who represents the district, appealed the ruling.<sup about=\"#mwt858\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-156\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-156\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-156\" id=\"mwBk0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBk4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBk8\">[</span>145<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBlA\">]</span></span></a></sup> On March 2, the U.S. Supreme Court temporarily blocked Pearlman's order, allowing the state's current map to be used for the 2026 election.<sup about=\"#mwt861\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-157\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-157\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-157\" id=\"mwBlE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBlI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBlM\">[</span>146<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBlQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwBlU\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt862\" id=\"mwBlY\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwBlc\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt863\" id=\"mwBlg\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwBlk\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt864\" id=\"mwBlo\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBls\">\n<th id=\"mwBlw\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#North_Carolina\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBl0\">North Carolina</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Yes\" style=\"background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-yes2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt865\" id=\"mwBl4\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=0 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ya\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ya\"},\"params\":{\"text\":{\"wt\":\"[[2025 North Carolina redistricting|New districts enacted]]\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_North_Carolina_redistricting\" title=\"2025 North Carolina redistricting\" class=\"mw-redirect\">New districts enacted</a></td>\n<td id=\"mwBl8\">The state Senate passed the bill for a new map making the competitive 1st congressional district more Republican-leaning on October 21, 2025. The state House passed it the next day. The governor, Josh Stein, does not have the authority to veto the map.<sup about=\"#mwt868\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-NCmap_115-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"NCmap\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NCmap-115\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-NCmap-115\" id=\"mwBmA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBmE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBmI\">[</span>105<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBmM\">]</span></span></a></sup> It has received pushback from the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NAACP\" title=\"NAACP\" id=\"mwBmQ\">NAACP</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Cause\" title=\"Common Cause\" id=\"mwBmU\">Common Cause</a>, both of which accused the new map of diluting the minority vote. A hearing was held on November 19 to consider blocking the map.<sup about=\"#mwt871\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-158\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-158\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-158\" id=\"mwBmY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBmc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBmg\">[</span>147<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBmk\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td id=\"mwBmo\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt872\" id=\"mwBms\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"steady\",\"href\":\"./Template:Steady\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td id=\"mwBmw\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt873\" id=\"mwBm0\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td>\n<td id=\"mwBm4\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt874\" id=\"mwBm8\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBnA\">\n<th id=\"mwBnE\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Ohio\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBnI\">Ohio</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Yes\" style=\"background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-yes2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt875\" id=\"mwBnM\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=0 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ya\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ya\"},\"params\":{\"text\":{\"wt\":\"New districts enacted\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>New districts enacted</td>\n<td id=\"mwBnQ\">Ohio voters amended the constitution in 2018, creating a process that requires both Republicans and Democrats in the state legislature to vote on the new congressional map. In the 2020 redistricting cycle, Democrats did not back a Republican proposal, necessitating a new map to be drawn in 2025. In October 2025, the Ohio Redistricting Commission passed a compromise map in a unanimous vote. The new map makes the 1st district more competitive, the 9th district lean more Republican, and the 13th district lean more Democratic.<sup about=\"#mwt878\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-OHnewmap_108-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"OHnewmap\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-OHnewmap-108\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-OHnewmap-108\" id=\"mwBnU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBnY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBnc\">[</span>98<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBng\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td id=\"mwBnk\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt879\" id=\"mwBno\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"steady\",\"href\":\"./Template:Steady\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td id=\"mwBns\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt880\" id=\"mwBnw\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 2</td>\n<td id=\"mwBn0\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt881\" id=\"mwBn4\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 2</td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBn8\">\n<th id=\"mwBoA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#South_Carolina\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBoE\">South Carolina</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"3\" style=\"background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-no2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt882\" id=\"mwBoI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=3 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"no2\",\"href\":\"./Template:No2\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Districts left in place\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>Districts left in place</td>\n<td id=\"mwBoM\">In June 2025, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Carolina_Supreme_Court\" title=\"South Carolina Supreme Court\" id=\"mwBoQ\">South Carolina Supreme Court</a> heard arguments in <i id=\"mwBoU\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/League_of_Women_Voters_of_South_Carolina_v._Alexander\" title=\"League of Women Voters of South Carolina v. Alexander\" id=\"mwBoY\">League of Women Voters v. Alexander</a></i>, as to whether the congressional maps are an unlawful partisan gerrymander in violation of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_South_Carolina\" title=\"Constitution of South Carolina\" id=\"mwBoc\">state's constitution</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt887\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-gm_159-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"gm\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-gm-159\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-gm-159\" id=\"mwBog\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBok\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBoo\">[</span>148<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBos\">]</span></span></a></sup> In September 2025, the court ruled that partisan gerrymandering is not in violation of the state's constitution, repeatedly referencing the 2019 SCOTUS case <i id=\"mwBow\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rucho_v._Common_Cause\" title=\"Rucho v. Common Cause\" id=\"mwBo0\">Rucho v. Common Cause</a></i>, leaving the current map in place.<sup about=\"#mwt888\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:0_103-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":0\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:0-103\" id=\"mwBo4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBo8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBpA\">[</span>93<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBpE\">]</span></span></a></sup><div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt883\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBpI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div><div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt884\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBpM\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>Following the U.S. Supreme Court's decision in <i id=\"mwBpQ\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_v._Callais\" title=\"Louisiana v. Callais\" id=\"mwBpU\">Louisiana v. Callais</a></i>, Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_McMaster\" title=\"Henry McMaster\" id=\"mwBpY\">Henry McMaster</a> called a special legislative session in May 2026 to consider redistricting and the state house approved a new map that would redraw the state's sole majority-minority district. However, the state senate ultimately voted against advancing the map after it became clear that passage would occur after the start of early voting in the state's primary election.<sup about=\"#mwt891\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-160\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-160\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-160\" id=\"mwBpc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBpg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBpk\">[</span>149<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBpo\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwBps\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt892\" id=\"mwBpw\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwBp0\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt893\" id=\"mwBp4\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwBp8\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt894\" id=\"mwBqA\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBqE\">\n<th id=\"mwBqI\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Tennessee\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBqM\">Tennessee</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Yes\" style=\"background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-yes2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt895\" id=\"mwBqQ\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=0 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ya\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ya\"},\"params\":{\"text\":{\"wt\":\"[[2026 Tennessee redistricting|New districts enacted]]\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Tennessee_redistricting\" title=\"2026 Tennessee redistricting\">New districts enacted</a></td>\n<td id=\"mwBqU\">In April 2026, the Supreme Court ruled on <i id=\"mwBqY\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_v._Callais\" title=\"Louisiana v. Callais\" id=\"mwBqc\">Louisiana v. Callais</a></i> that stricter scrutiny had to be applied with regard to section 2 of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voting_Rights_Act\" title=\"Voting Rights Act\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBqg\">Voting Rights Act</a>. After facing calls to redistrict from U.S. Senator <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsha_Blackburn\" title=\"Marsha Blackburn\" id=\"mwBqk\">Marsha Blackburn</a> and U.S. President <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump\" title=\"Donald Trump\" id=\"mwBqo\">Donald Trump</a>, Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Lee_(Tennessee_politician)\" title=\"Bill Lee (Tennessee politician)\" id=\"mwBqs\">Bill Lee</a> called a special session to redraw the sole majority-minority district in Tennessee.<sup about=\"#mwt898\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-161\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-161\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-161\" id=\"mwBqw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBq0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBq4\">[</span>150<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBq8\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwBrA\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt899\" id=\"mwBrE\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwBrI\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt900\" id=\"mwBrM\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"steady\",\"href\":\"./Template:Steady\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwBrQ\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt901\" id=\"mwBrU\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBrY\">\n<th id=\"mwBrc\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Texas\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBrg\">Texas</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Yes\" style=\"background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-yes2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt902\" id=\"mwBrk\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=0 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ya\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ya\"},\"params\":{\"text\":{\"wt\":\"[[2025 Texas redistricting|New districts enacted]]\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Texas_redistricting\" title=\"2025 Texas redistricting\">New districts enacted</a></td>\n<td id=\"mwBro\">In <i id=\"mwBrs\">League of United Latin American Citizens v. Abbott</i>, held from May to June 2025 in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_District_Court_for_the_Western_District_of_Texas\" title=\"United States District Court for the Western District of Texas\" id=\"mwBrw\">U.S. District Court for the Western District of Texas</a>, plaintiffs argued that the congressional districts passed by the state legislature discriminated against Black and Latino voters in violation of the Voting Rights Act.<sup about=\"#mwt908\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-162\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-162\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-162\" id=\"mwBr0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBr4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBr8\">[</span>151<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBsA\">]</span></span></a></sup><div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt903\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBsE\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div><div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt904\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBsI\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>In early 2025, the Trump Administration urged Texas officials to redraw congressional districts. This was followed by a meeting of the Texas Republican congressional delegation to discuss mid-decade redistricting to secure extra Republican seats.<sup about=\"#mwt911\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-163\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-163\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-163\" id=\"mwBsM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBsQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBsU\">[</span>152<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBsY\">]</span></span></a></sup> On July 9, Governor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Abbott\" title=\"Greg Abbott\" id=\"mwBsc\">Greg Abbott</a> called a special session of the legislature to be held later that month with the goal of creating 5 new Republican seats. After Texas House Democrats staged a weeks-long walkout, the legislature passed the new maps on August 23, and Abbott signed them into law on August 29.<sup about=\"#mwt912\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-tg_109-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"tg\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-tg-109\" id=\"mwBsg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBsk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBso\">[</span>99<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBss\">]</span></span></a></sup><div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt905\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBsw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div> The previous case was paused, pending new maps.<sup about=\"#mwt913\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-LULAC_105-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"LULAC\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-LULAC-105\" id=\"mwBs0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBs4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBs8\">[</span>95<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBtA\">]</span></span></a></sup> After passage, on August 27, the court scheduled a preliminary injunction hearing to begin on October 1 to October 10.<sup about=\"#mwt916\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-oh_164-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"oh\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-oh-164\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-oh-164\" id=\"mwBtE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBtI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBtM\">[</span>153<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBtQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> On November 18, the panel issued a preliminary injunction blocking the new map, putting the former map back in place. The case on the 2021 maps remains open, pending action from the U.S. Supreme Court in <i id=\"mwBtU\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_v._Callais\" title=\"Louisiana v. Callais\" id=\"mwBtY\">Louisiana v. Callais</a></i>.<sup about=\"#mwt917\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:5_110-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":5\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:5-110\" id=\"mwBtc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBtg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBtk\">[</span>100<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBto\">]</span></span></a></sup> On November 21, the U.S. Supreme Court issued an administrative stay on the lower court ruling, temporarily leaving the new map in place.<sup about=\"#mwt918\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-TXmap_111-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"TXmap\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-TXmap-111\" id=\"mwBts\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBtw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBt0\">[</span>101<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBt4\">]</span></span></a></sup> On December 4, the Supreme Court ruled 6–3 in allowing the map to stand for the 2026 elections.<sup about=\"#mwt921\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-165\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-165\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-165\" id=\"mwBt8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBuA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBuE\">[</span>154<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBuI\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwBuM\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt922\" id=\"mwBuQ\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 3</td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwBuU\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt923\" id=\"mwBuY\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 2</td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwBuc\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt924\" id=\"mwBug\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 5</td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBuk\">\n<th id=\"mwBuo\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Utah\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBus\">Utah</a></th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"Yes\" style=\"background: #DFD; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-yes2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt925\" id=\"mwBuw\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|data-sort-value=0 \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ya\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ya\"},\"params\":{\"text\":{\"wt\":\"New districts enacted\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>New districts enacted</td>\n<td id=\"mwBu0\">In July 2023, in <i id=\"mwBu4\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/League_of_Women_Voters_v._Utah_State_Legislature\" title=\"League of Women Voters v. Utah State Legislature\" id=\"mwBu8\">League of Women Voters v. Utah State Legislature</a></i>, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utah_Supreme_Court\" title=\"Utah Supreme Court\" id=\"mwBvA\">Utah Supreme Court</a> heard arguments alleging that the Utah Legislature violated <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_Utah_Proposition_4\" title=\"2018 Utah Proposition 4\" id=\"mwBvE\">a citizen-passed anti-gerrymandering proposition</a> by dividing Salt Lake County voters into all four of Utah's districts. The case was sent back to a state district court, which held a hearing in January 2025. A ruling for the League of Women Voters was issued on August 25. New maps were expected to be drawn up by the Legislature by September 24 and finalized by November.<sup about=\"#mwt928\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-redrawn_166-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"redrawn\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-redrawn-166\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-redrawn-166\" id=\"mwBvI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBvM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBvQ\">[</span>155<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBvU\">]</span></span></a></sup>\n<div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt929\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBvY\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>On October 6, the Utah Legislature passed a new map, which changed 2 Republican districts to be more competitive.<sup about=\"#mwt932\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:2_167-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":2\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:2-167\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:2-167\" id=\"mwBvc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBvg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBvk\">[</span>156<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBvo\">]</span></span></a></sup> On November 10, Utah Third District Judge Dianna Gibson ruled that the new map also violated Proposition 4, opting to approve a plaintiff-submitted alternative, Map 1, which creates a safe Democratic district comprising only <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_Lake_County\" title=\"Salt Lake County\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBvs\">Salt Lake County</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt933\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-:4_106-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\":4\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-:4-106\" id=\"mwBvw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBv0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBv4\">[</span>96<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBv8\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td id=\"mwBwA\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt934\" id=\"mwBwE\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"increase\",\"href\":\"./Template:Increase\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td>\n<td id=\"mwBwI\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt935\" id=\"mwBwM\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"steady\",\"href\":\"./Template:Steady\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td id=\"mwBwQ\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt936\" id=\"mwBwU\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"decrease\",\"href\":\"./Template:Decrease\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwBwY\">\n<th id=\"mwBwc\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Virginia\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwBwg\">Virginia</a></th>\n<td style=\"background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-no2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt937\" id=\"mwBwk\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"no2\",\"href\":\"./Template:No2\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Districts left in place\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>Districts left in place</td>\n<td id=\"mwBwo\">Democratic state lawmakers announced a plan to alter the state constitution to draw a new congressional map before the 2026 elections making 3-4 more Democratic seats.<sup about=\"#mwt938\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-auto_120-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"auto\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-auto-120\" id=\"mwBws\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBww\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBw0\">[</span>110<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBw4\">]</span></span></a></sup>\n<div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt939\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBw8\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>The proposed mechanism was an amendment to the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Virginia\" title=\"Constitution of Virginia\" id=\"mwBxA\">Constitution of Virginia</a> allowing the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_General_Assembly\" title=\"Virginia General Assembly\" id=\"mwBxE\">General Assembly</a> to modify the state's congressional districts if any other state did so between January 1, 2025 and October 31, 2030 for any reason other than normal decennial redistricting or to satisfy a court order. Redistricting was transferred from the General Assembly to a bipartisan commission in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_Virginia_Question_1\" title=\"2020 Virginia Question 1\" id=\"mwBxI\">2020</a>, and the power would revert to the commission for the normal 2030 cycle. The amendment proposal first passed the General Assembly on October 31, 2025. The amendment procedure requires any proposal to pass in both houses of the General Assembly, then it must pass both houses again after the next <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_House_of_Delegates\" title=\"Virginia House of Delegates\" id=\"mwBxM\">Virginia House of Delegates</a> election is held (every two years), then it must be approved in a referendum.<sup about=\"#mwt942\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-168\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-168\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-168\" id=\"mwBxQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBxU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBxY\">[</span>157<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBxc\">]</span></span></a></sup>  \n\n<p id=\"mwBxg\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_Senate\" title=\"Virginia Senate\" id=\"mwBxk\">Virginia Senate</a> minority leader <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryan_McDougle\" title=\"Ryan McDougle\" id=\"mwBxo\">Ryan McDougle</a>, a Republican, sued Democratic House Speaker <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_Scott_(Virginia_politician)\" title=\"Don Scott (Virginia politician)\" id=\"mwBxs\">Don Scott</a> over the legality of the amendment. On January 27, 2026, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tazewell_County,_Virginia\" title=\"Tazewell County, Virginia\" id=\"mwBxw\">Tazewell County</a> Circuit Court Judge Jack Hurley, Jr. ruled that the amendment could not satisfy the intervening-election requirement since early voting in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Virginia_elections\" title=\"2025 Virginia elections\" id=\"mwBx0\">2025 Virginia elections</a> was underway at the time of passage.<sup about=\"#mwt945\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-169\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-169\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-169\" id=\"mwBx4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBx8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByA\">[</span>158<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByE\">]</span></span></a></sup> On January 28, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_of_Virginia\" title=\"Democratic Party of Virginia\" id=\"mwByI\">Democratic Party of Virginia</a> appealed the ruling; the court of appeals, citing the importance of the case, forwarded it to the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_Virginia\" title=\"Supreme Court of Virginia\" id=\"mwByM\">Supreme Court of Virginia</a> for an expedited ruling on February 4.<sup about=\"#mwt948\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-170\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-170\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-170\" id=\"mwByQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwByU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByY\">[</span>159<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByc\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt951\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-171\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-171\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-171\" id=\"mwByg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwByk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByo\">[</span>160<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBys\">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 10, the General Assembly passed the amendment proposal the required second time and included a draft map that would likely net Democrats four seats.<sup about=\"#mwt954\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-172\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-172\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-172\" id=\"mwByw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBy0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBy4\">[</span>161<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBy8\">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 13, the Supreme Court allowed the April 21 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Virginia_redistricting_amendment\" title=\"2026 Virginia redistricting amendment\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBzA\">referendum</a> to go forward while it considered the matter. The referendum passed with 51.7% voting yes.<sup about=\"#mwt957\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-173\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-173\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-173\" id=\"mwBzE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBzI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBzM\">[</span>162<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBzQ\">]</span></span></a></sup>  The next day, Judge Hurley ruled the referendum to be unconstitutional on the basis of another lawsuit and enjoined the state board of elections from certifying the result. Attorney General <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_Jones\" title=\"Jay Jones\" id=\"mwBzU\">Jay Jones</a> appealed the decision; the Supreme Court declined to stay it while the original case was ongoing and as a result the board was unable to certify the result at its May meeting.<sup about=\"#mwt960\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-174\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-174\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-174\" id=\"mwBzY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBzc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBzg\">[</span>163<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBzk\">]</span></span></a></sup> <sup about=\"#mwt963\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-175\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-175\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-175\" id=\"mwBzo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBzs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBzw\">[</span>164<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBz0\">]</span></span></a></sup> The Supreme Court heard oral arguments in the case on April 27.<sup about=\"#mwt966\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-176\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-176\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-176\" id=\"mwBz4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBz8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0A\">[</span>165<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0E\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \n\nOn May 8, the Supreme Court invalidated the amendment in a 4–3 decision, with the majority agreeing with Judge Hurley's ruling that its first passage was too late to satisfy the intervening-election requirement.<sup about=\"#mwt970\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-177\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-177\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-177\" id=\"mwB0I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB0M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0Q\">[</span>166<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0U\">]</span></span></a></sup><div class=\"paragraphbreak\" style=\"margin-top:0.5em\" about=\"#mwt967\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB0Y\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"pb\",\"href\":\"./Template:Pb\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'></div>Following the ruling, Speaker Scott and Attorney General Jones filed an emergency appeal to the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Supreme_Court\" title=\"United States Supreme Court\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB0c\">United States Supreme Court</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt973\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-178\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-178\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-178\" id=\"mwB0g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB0k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0o\">[</span>167<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0s\">]</span></span></a></sup> On May 15, the Supreme Court denied the appeal.<sup about=\"#mwt976\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-179\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-179\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-179\" id=\"mwB0w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB00\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB04\">[</span>168<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB08\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwB1A\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt977\" id=\"mwB1E\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwB1I\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt978\" id=\"mwB1M\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwB1Q\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt979\" id=\"mwB1U\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td></tr>\n<tr id=\"mwB1Y\">\n<th id=\"mwB1c\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#Wisconsin\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwB1g\">Wisconsin</a></th>\n<td style=\"background: #FFE3E3; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; \" class=\"table-no2 skin-invert\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt980\" id=\"mwB1k\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[\"|\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"no2\",\"href\":\"./Template:No2\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Districts left in place\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>Districts left in place</td>\n<td id=\"mwB1o\">In July 2025, a lawsuit was filed by two liberal law firms in a Wisconsin district court, asking to consider the constitutionality of Wisconsin's congressional maps.<sup about=\"#mwt983\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-180\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-180\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-180\" id=\"mwB1s\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB1w\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB10\">[</span>169<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB14\">]</span></span></a></sup> In September 2025, the Wisconsin Supreme court addressed this lawsuit and asked each party to provide briefs on whether this court case should proceed.<sup about=\"#mwt986\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-181\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-181\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-181\" id=\"mwB18\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB2A\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2E\">[</span>170<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2I\">]</span></span></a></sup> On March 31, 2026, a judicial panel dismissed the challenge.<sup about=\"#mwt989\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-182\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw='{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-182\"}}'><a href=\"#cite_note-182\" id=\"mwB2M\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB2Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2U\">[</span>171<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2Y\">]</span></span></a></sup></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" id=\"mwB2c\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt990\" id=\"mwB2g\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"0\" id=\"mwB2k\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt991\" id=\"mwB2o\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"−1\" id=\"mwB2s\"><span typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:File\" about=\"#mwt992\" id=\"mwB2w\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Steady\",\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Same\",\"href\":\"./Template:Same\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}'><span title=\"Steady\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Steady2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/20px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Steady2.svg/40px-Steady2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Steady\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"sortbottom\" id=\"mwB20\">\n<th colspan=\"3\" id=\"mwB24\">Net change <span style=\"font-size: 85%;\" about=\"#mwt993\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB28\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"small\",\"href\":\"./Template:Small\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"(as of {{date|2=MDY}})\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'>(as of October 15, 2026)</span></th>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\" id=\"mwB3A\"><span class=\"nowrap\" about=\"#mwt994\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB3E\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"nowrap\",\"href\":\"./Template:Nowrap\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"{{increase}} 1\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><span typeof=\"mw:File\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\"}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 1</span></td>\n<td id=\"mwB3I\"><span class=\"nowrap\" about=\"#mwt995\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB3M\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"nowrap\",\"href\":\"./Template:Nowrap\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"{{decrease}} 13\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><span typeof=\"mw:File\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Decrease\"}'><span title=\"Decrease\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Decrease2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/20px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Decrease2.svg/40px-Decrease2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Decrease\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 13</span></td>\n<td id=\"mwB3Q\"><span class=\"nowrap\" about=\"#mwt996\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB3U\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"nowrap\",\"href\":\"./Template:Nowrap\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"{{increase}} 12\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><span typeof=\"mw:File\" data-mw='{\"caption\":\"Increase\"}'><span title=\"Increase\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Increase2.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/20px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Increase2.svg/40px-Increase2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"Increase\" data-file-width=\"300\" data-file-height=\"300\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"11\" width=\"11\" class=\"mw-file-element\"/></span></span> 12</span></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"20\" id=\"mwB3Y\" aria-labelledby=\"Newly_created_seats\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Newly_created_seats\">Newly created seats</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Newly created seats\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p id=\"mwB3c\">The following districts had no incumbent representative as a result of redistricting.</p>\n\n<ol id=\"mwB3g\"><li id=\"mwB3k\"><span data-sort-value=\"Alabama01 !\" about=\"#mwt997\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB3o\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"AL\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alabama's_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Alabama's 1st congressional district\">Alabama<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>1</a></span></li>\n<li id=\"mwB3s\"><span data-sort-value=\"California38 !\" about=\"#mwt998\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB3w\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"CA\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"38\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California's_38th_congressional_district\" title=\"California's 38th congressional district\">California<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>38</a></span></li>\n<li id=\"mwB30\"><span data-sort-value=\"Florida22 !\" about=\"#mwt999\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB34\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"FL\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"22\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Florida's_22nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Florida's 22nd congressional district\">Florida<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>22</a></span></li>\n<li id=\"mwB38\"><span data-sort-value=\"Texas09 !\" about=\"#mwt1000\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB4A\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"TX\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"9\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas's_9th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas's 9th congressional district\">Texas<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>9</a></span></li>\n<li id=\"mwB4E\"><span data-sort-value=\"Texas30 !\" about=\"#mwt1001\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB4I\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"TX\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"30\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas's_30th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas's 30th congressional district\">Texas<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>30</a></span></li>\n<li id=\"mwB4M\"><span data-sort-value=\"Texas32 !\" about=\"#mwt1002\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB4Q\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"TX\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"32\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas's_32nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas's 32nd congressional district\">Texas<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>32</a></span></li>\n<li id=\"mwB4U\"><span data-sort-value=\"Texas35 !\" about=\"#mwt1003\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB4Y\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"TX\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"35\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas's_35th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas's 35th congressional district\">Texas<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>35</a></span></li>\n<li id=\"mwB4c\"><span data-sort-value=\"Utah01 !\" about=\"#mwt1004\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB4g\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"UT\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"X\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utah's_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Utah's 1st congressional district\">Utah<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>1</a></span></li></ol>\n\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"21\" id=\"mwB4k\" aria-labelledby=\"Seats_with_multiple_incumbents_running\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Seats_with_multiple_incumbents_running\">Seats with multiple incumbents running</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Seats with multiple incumbents running\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p id=\"mwB4o\">The following districts will have multiple incumbent representatives running, a product of multiple districts merging in redistricting.</p>\n\n<ol id=\"mwB4s\"><li id=\"mwB4w\"><span data-sort-value=\"California40 !\" about=\"#mwt1005\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB40\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"CA\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"40\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"x\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California's_40th_congressional_district\" title=\"California's 40th congressional district\">California<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>40</a></span>: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Calvert\" title=\"Ken Calvert\" id=\"mwB44\">Ken Calvert</a> (R) and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Young_Kim\" title=\"Young Kim\" id=\"mwB48\">Young Kim</a> (R)</li>\n<li id=\"mwB5A\"><span data-sort-value=\"Texas18 !\" about=\"#mwt1006\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB5E\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"ushr\",\"href\":\"./Template:Ushr\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"TX\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"18\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"x\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Texas's_18th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas's 18th congressional district\">Texas<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\"> </span>18</a></span>: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Menefee\" title=\"Christian Menefee\" id=\"mwB5I\">Christian Menefee</a> (D) defeated <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Green_(politician)\" title=\"Al Green (politician)\" id=\"mwB5M\">Al Green</a> (D)</li></ol>\n\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"22\" id=\"mwB5Q\" aria-labelledby=\"Election_ratings\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Election_ratings\">Election ratings</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2026_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Election ratings\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1007\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB5U\" data-mw='{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"2026 United States House of Representatives election ratings\"}},\"i\":0}}]}'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicate